# Store everything with LF in the repository.
#
# This matters for start.sh specifically: committed from Windows without this,
# it would arrive on macOS and Linux with CRLF endings, where the shell reads
# the trailing \r as part of the interpreter path and fails with a confusing
# "bad interpreter" error. The one file meant for non-Windows users would be
# the one file that did not work.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Windows launchers are the exception - cmd and wscript want CRLF.
*.vbs text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Leave binaries alone entirely.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
